Date: Sun, 7 Jun 2026 11:07:04 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 00814/11362] [outer-loop] Strongest-prompt judge panel: energy
 STILL dominates (efficiency axis closed)

Boosted few-shot + structured-self-check prompt (the exp3916 0.663-capable prompt)
across all 4 local SOTA judges, n=528:
  Qwen3.6-35B-A3B  0.729 (best judge; few-shot lifted it from 0.640)
  gemma-4-26B-A4B  0.637 (lifted from 0.449 -> confirms prompt framing matters)
  gemma-4-12B-it   0.603
  gemma-4-31B-it   0.412 (few-shot did not help this model)
Energy verifier 0.810 STILL beats every judge at the strongest prompt, 6,077-49,825x
cheaper. The 'you hobbled the judge' objection is now closed: few-shot + structured
self-check + 160tok/2048ctx, and the best SOTA local judge (0.729) still loses to
the energy verifier at >6000x lower cost. Efficiency-axis verifier moat: demonstrated.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
